{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"0e6629ee-3e9b-4f79-bef6-06da7530a002","runId":"33481928-71b6-4b21-a893-d975a6e94192","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:c72948e56909aaddc8ffc3439c87dc34c103189d856ab69e1dcb3a9f900999e2","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a043bc-89ea-77fc-97ec-9b717d9ac238","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T15:03:26.712Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verdict | **Confirmed** |\n| Confidence | **High** |\n| Severity | **Medium** |\n| Task Type | Security regression hardening |\n\n### What Was Claimed\n\nPR #199 removed the positive safe-integer validation from `GitHubIssueProjector.setWorkflowLabel`, permitting malformed runtime values to be interpolated into GitHub issue API paths.\n\n### What We Found\n\nThe frozen `staging` base already contains both an explicit safe-integer guard in `setWorkflowLabel` and a shared `requireIssueNumber` guard at the start of `#replaceWorkflowLabel`, before path construction. The unsafe behavior therefore does not reproduce at the frozen base. However, the focused adapter tests do not assert rejection of malformed runtime issue numbers or prove that the transport remains untouched, leaving the reviewed regression without durable coverage.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe label-projection tests exercise valid workflow transitions but omit the runtime boundary for `issueNumber`. That omission allowed the validation regression identified at the source PR head and leaves future refactors able to remove the guard unnoticed.\n\n### Affected Files\n\n| File | Reason |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/adapters/github-projection.ts` | Owns validation before GitHub issue-path interpolation. |\n| `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` | Lacks focused malformed-issue-number regression coverage. |\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `requireIssueNumber` rejects values that are not positive safe integers.\n- `setWorkflowLabel` currently rejects invalid issue numbers before delegating.\n- `#replaceWorkflowLabel` also calls `requireIssueNumber` before constructing `issuePath` or `labelsPath`.\n- Existing workflow-label tests only use issue number `42` and do not assert a zero-transport failure path.\n\n### History Findings\n\nThe finding originated from security review of PR #199 at head `a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`. The frozen integration base `b7bfc323d992812b772c0cedce76b95a17922caa` has restored validation, but no focused regression test records the safety requirement.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nConsolidate `setWorkflowLabel` on the shared validator and add a focused test covering malformed runtime values, including path-like strings, while asserting no GitHub transport request occurs.\n\n### Related Issues\n\n- PR/issue reference `#199` supplied by the review-finding artifact.\n\n### Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The change is isolated to one adapter method and its focused test file.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- [x] Validate the review finding against the current integration base.\n- [ ] Ensure `setWorkflowLabel` rejects every non-positive-safe-integer value before transport access.\n- [ ] Add focused regression coverage for numeric and path-like malformed values.\n- [ ] Run the required `check` verification command.\n- [ ] Re-review the exact remediation head with correctness and security reviewers.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->"}}
