{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"faf4f1cb-5075-4e5b-91af-a561ab6aa6c9","runId":"33481928-71b6-4b21-a893-d975a6e94192","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":19,"previousEventHash":"sha256:35876dd37744e30c3dbfbcd1b7cd9aedf93a4c9d240760c627235786066c594d","type":"effect.recorded","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a043bc-89ea-77fc-97ec-9b717d9ac238","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T15:04:34.011Z","idempotencyKey":"effect:github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:209:8f90e17d-2e46-4582-a0af-0eeefdba9af9","payload":{"effectType":"github-label","effectId":"github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:209:8f90e17d-2e46-4582-a0af-0eeefdba9af9","digest":"sha256:a20143e54004909c7ea3e29042335c7b61dca609df97a122f1275197d775deee"}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"2da05c24-e6db-43fa-894a-0016df55586a","runId":"33481928-71b6-4b21-a893-d975a6e94192","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":20,"previousEventHash":"sha256:4fbf667b349264b35f22d163a1b4c01b9eecfca65810424fc94a9cf2d88036f0","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a043bc-89ea-77fc-97ec-9b717d9ac238","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T15:05:14.514Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:CONTRACT -->\n## Builder Contract\n\n### Objective\n\nMake the workflow-label issue-number trust boundary explicit and durable without changing valid label-projection behavior.\n\n### Allowed Paths\n\n- `src/adapters/github-projection.ts`\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts`\n\n### Forbidden Changes\n\n- GitHub API routes, label mutation semantics, or receipt formats.\n- Public API signatures or workflow authority behavior.\n- Verification policy, repository configuration, dependencies, or unrelated tests.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- Invalid issue numbers fail before any transport request.\n- Valid positive safe integers retain existing behavior.\n- Workflow-label validation and unrelated-label preservation remain unchanged.\n- No credentials, private artifacts, or production data enter fixtures.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Reuse the shared issue-number validator in `setWorkflowLabel`.\n- Add focused malformed runtime value coverage with a zero-transport assertion.\n- Pass the required `check` command.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC-2:** `setWorkflowLabel` rejects malformed runtime issue numbers before transport access.\n- [ ] **AC-3:** Coverage includes non-positive, non-integer, unsafe, and path-like runtime values.\n- [ ] **AC-4:** Required `check` verification passes.\n- [ ] **AC-5:** Fresh correctness and security reviewers approve the frozen remediation head.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT -->\n## Implementation Context\n\n### History\n\n- Security review finding `security-001` identified the regression at PR #199 head `a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`.\n- Frozen base `b7bfc323d992812b772c0cedce76b95a17922caa` has restored guards but lacks focused regression coverage.\n\n### Callers and Data Flow\n\n- Workflow coordinators call `GitHubIssueProjector.setWorkflowLabel(issueNumber, label)`.\n- The method validates inputs and delegates to `#replaceWorkflowLabel`.\n- `#replaceWorkflowLabel` constructs issue and label paths, mutates Forge-owned labels, performs fresh read-back, and creates a receipt.\n\n### CI Surface\n\n- `npm run check` runs TypeScript type checking and the complete Node test suite.\n- Focused adapter coverage lives in `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts`.\n\n### Prior Findings\n\n- Path/query characters can reach the transport if a deserialized or JavaScript caller bypasses the TypeScript annotation and validation is absent.\n- The current shared private guard protects all workflow-label projection paths.\n\n### Hazards\n\n- A test that only expects rejection without checking transport calls could miss validation that occurs after path construction or I/O.\n- Broad changes to other projection methods would expand scope unnecessarily.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT:COMPLETE -->\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT -->\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Replace the duplicate inline `setWorkflowLabel` check with the existing shared `requireIssueNumber` validator.\n2. Add a parameterized adapter regression test that passes representative malformed runtime values and asserts the exact `TypeError`.\n3. Instrument the transport in that test and assert zero calls, proving rejection precedes GitHub path access.\n4. Run the trusted `check` verification command and commit through the bound Forge tool.\n5. Prepare the PR, freeze its head, and run the required fresh correctness and security panel.\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Altering `setWorkflowLabelWithReceipt`, clear-label methods, or private replacement logic.\n- Changing label names, mutation ordering, API request shapes, or receipt identity.\n- Addressing unrelated projection input-validation gaps.\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT:COMPLETE -->"}}
